import{f as a,g as t,i as e,j as i,k as o,u as n,l as s,m as r,R as l}from"./index-6a625f00.js";const c={class:"mission pageWrapper"},d=e("div",{class:"heroImage"},null,-1),u={class:"heroContent"},h=e("p",{class:"title"},"Our mission",-1),g=e("p",null," Our primary mission is to bridge the gap between classroom education and global awareness by providing an open, accessible platform for geographical discovery. In an increasingly interconnected world, understanding the diverse cultures, borders, and histories of different nations is no longer just an academic requirement—it is a vital skill for global citizenship. By offering an intuitive and visually engaging environment, we aim to inspire students and educators alike to look beyond geopolitical boundaries and foster a genuine appreciation for the rich tapestry of our shared planet. ",-1),p=e("p",null," Through our proud partnership with UNESCO, we are deeply committed to promoting heritage preservation and cultural literacy on a global scale. We believe that education is the most powerful tool for creating sustainable peace, and by teaching people about the unique stories behind every flag and border, we help safeguard the world's intangible heritage. Our platform serves as a digital gateway that empowers individuals to explore the globe responsibly, encouraging a lifelong passion for learning, intercultural dialogue, and environmental stewardship. ",-1),m=s('<div class="imageWrapper first"></div><div class="unescoWrapper"><div class="text"><p class="subtitle">UNESCO &amp; InfoSchool Partnership</p><p> The roots of UNESCO trace back to 1942, during the height of World War II, when European governments met for the Conference of Allied Ministers of Education. They sought ways to rebuild their educational systems once peace was restored. This collaborative initiative quickly gained global momentum, culminating in the official founding of the United Nations Educational, Scientific and Cultural Organization in November 1945, with a foundational mandate to build peace in the minds of men and women. </p><p> Over the decades, UNESCO has evolved into a global guardian of human knowledge and cultural heritage. From launching massive literacy campaigns in the mid-20th century to establishing the historic World Heritage Convention in 1972, the organization has consistently worked to protect the world&#39;s most vulnerable treasures. Today, its efforts span across science, environmental preservation, and digital inclusivity, ensuring that historical milestones and natural wonders survive the pressures of modern development. </p><p> In alignment with these global values, InfoSchool has established a proud partnership with UNESCO to revolutionize how geography and cultural history are taught in the digital age. By combining UNESCO&#39;s unparalleled database of global heritage with our interactive educational tools, we have transformed raw statistical data into a vibrant, visual learning experience. This collaboration allows us to bring authentic, verified cultural narratives directly to students, closing the gap between traditional textbooks and modern digital classrooms. </p><p> Through the InfoSchool platform, this partnership aims to cultivate a new generation of globally conscious citizens who value cultural literacy and international peace. By exploring the unique stories, flags, and backgrounds of different countries on our site, users are not just memorizing maps—they are actively engaging with the shared heritage of humanity. Together with UNESCO, InfoSchool is committed to making comprehensive global education accessible, engaging, and inspiring for learners everywhere. </p><p><a href="https://www.unesco.org/en" target="_blank"> Visit the UNESCO official site </a></p></div><div class="unescoImage"></div></div>',2),y={__name:"Mission",setup(f){return(v,b)=>(a(),t("div",c,[d,e("div",u,[h,g,p,e("p",null,[i(n(l),{to:"/countries"},{default:o(()=>[r(" Learn about countries here ")]),_:1})]),m])]))}};export{y as default};
